      "corroboration": "NONE_ON_DISK",
      "what_it_said": "three substantive findings: (critical) this result dossier's hash differs from the hash bound by the protocol verdict, suspected byte drift; (major) section 7 claims every case directory carries admission_certificate.json but the 18 coarse directories do not; (major) o1_result.json's cost.note says the 108 equivalent bill is three times the support block, while 108 = 3 x 36 is the whole bill tripled",
      "why_there_is_no_file": "the harness at that time wrote a5_result_review/verdict.json in place, so the next round overwrote it; the per-round copy into rounds/ was added afterwards.  The only surviving trace is the generator stdout, which is no longer retrievable either.",
      "how_a_reader_should_weight_it": "as a disclosure, not as evidence: it is listed here so that nobody can accuse the record of pretending the round never happened, and it is marked NONE_ON_DISK so that nobody can mistake it for something they can verify"
    }
  ],
  "rule": "a result-level verdict speaks only for the dossier bytes it names; every round is kept as its own dated file, and a round that left no file is listed as uncorroborated rather than omitted",
